summary:
  A country pinned while the chip rail is switched off fences every later search.

history:
  The country chip and the ✕ that releases it live on the discovery rail,
  and Appearance can take the rail away. "jazz in uk" then pinned Britain
  unseen and "raadio elmar" found nothing, with no way to see why. A hidden
  rail hands the search no fence; this takes that sentence out.

target:
  package/contents/ui/SearchLogic.js

find:
      if (s.countryRole || s.railShown === false) return "";

replace:
      if (s.countryRole) return "";

expect:
  Killed by tst_searchlogic::test_a_hidden_rail_never_fences_a_later_search.
  Line-neutral.
